"""Micras encoder slot: the main board's side of the board-to-board joint with an encoder board.

The encoder board (components/micras/EncoderTab) stands upright in a slot in the
main board, and its tab pads are soldered to 8 pads on the main board's top side,
4 on each side of the slot. Pad n here meets encoder tab pad n:

| Pad | Signal | Encoder tab side |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | CSn | bottom (pads 1-4) |
| 2 | CLK | bottom |
| 3 | MISO | bottom |
| 4 | MOSI | bottom |
| 5 | VDD (3.3 V) | top, chip side (pads 5-8) |
| 6 | GND | top |
| 7 | A | top |
| 8 | B | top |

Geometry:
- Pads 1.0 x 0.6 mm, 0.95 mm pitch along the slot (Y), the same pitch and
  0.6 mm width as the tab pads (pad size and pitch from the Altium MicrasLib
  ENCODER_CONNECTOR). Pads 1-4 at x = -1.21 mm, pads 5-8 at x = +1.21 mm, both
  rows from y = -1.425 mm (pads 1, 5) to y = +1.425 mm (pads 4, 8). Inner pad
  edges at x = +/-0.71 mm, 0.21 mm from the slot wall, above the 0.20 mm
  copper-to-edge minimum of rules/jlcpcb.kicad_dru.
- The slot is 1.0 mm wide and 5.8 mm long with fully rounded ends (0.5 mm
  radius), on the board's Edge.Cuts, centred on the footprint origin and long
  along Y. It is board outline, not part of this footprint (the footprint
  draws it on F.Fab only), so the board's mechanical spec must place it with
  the footprint.
- The encoder board's chip side faces +X: seen from that side, tab pad 5
  (u = +1.425 mm in spec/encoder.toml's frame) lands at y = -1.425 mm, on pad 5.

Slot size (JLCPCB PCB capabilities, jlcpcb.com/capabilities/pcb-capabilities,
read 2026-10-14): a non-plated slot is at least 1.0 mm wide and is milled, so
its ends are rounded with at least half the slot width. Fit against
spec/encoder.toml: the 0.79 mm encoder board (up to 0.89 mm with JLCPCB's
+-0.1 mm thickness tolerance below 1.0 mm) in the 1.0 mm slot; the 5.0 mm tab's
corners (+/-2.5, +/-0.445) lie 0.46 mm from the centres (+/-2.4, 0) of the
0.5 mm end radii, inside the rounded ends (tests/test_spec.py checks the fit at
the worst case of both boards' tolerances). The encoder board's 8.0 mm shoulder rests on
the board top 1.1 mm beyond each slot end.

Not a purchased part: copper and a cut-out on the main board, so it is excluded
from the BOM and the placement file.
"""

load("@stdlib/interfaces.zen", "Spi")

# AS5047U DS v1-00 Figure 6: VDD = VDD3V3 = 3.0-3.6 V in 3.3 V mode, the mode the
# encoder board runs in (components/ams/AS5047U).
VDD = io(Power(voltage="3.0V to 3.6V"))
GND = io(Ground)
SPI = io(Spi)
A = io(Net)
B = io(Net)

Component(
    name="SLOT",
    prefix="EC",
    symbol=Symbol(library="EncoderSlot.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("EncoderSlot_2x4_P0.95mm.kicad_mod"),
    pins={
        "CSn": SPI.CS,
        "CLK": SPI.CLK,
        "MISO": SPI.MISO,
        "MOSI": SPI.MOSI,
        "VDD": VDD,
        "GND": GND,
        "A": A,
        "B": B,
    },
    skip_bom=True,
)
